<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>Stocks-Markets-Economic Times</title><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks</link><description><![CDATA[Stock Market News: Latest Stock news and updates on The Economic Times. Find Stock Market Live Updates, BSE, NSE Top Gainers, Losers and more.]]> </description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:58:37 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/2146842.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) 2026 Bennett Coleman and Co. Ltd, http://info.indiatimes.com/terms/tou.html</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>Economic Times</title><url>https://img.etimg.com/thumb/msid-76939477,width-600,height-60/economictimes.jpg</url><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[PE/VC investments in India surge to USD 8.7 billion in October, highest monthly level in five years: EY-IVCA report]]> </title><description><![CDATA[Private equity and venture capital investments in India surged to USD 8.7 billion in October 2026. This monthly figure is the highest recorded in the past five years, supported by eight large deals totaling USD 7.3 billion. Financial services attracted the majority of investments, amounting to USD 5.9 billion during this period. Despite the increase in investments, exit activity declined, with 21 exits valued at USD 544 million.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/pe/vc-investments-in-india-surge-to-usd-8-7-billion-in-october-highest-monthly-level-in-five-years-ey-ivca-report/articleshow/136132831.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-136132831,imgsize-47450.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/pe/vc-investments-in-india-surge-to-usd-8-7-billion-in-october-highest-monthly-level-in-five-years-ey-ivca-report/articleshow/136132831.cms</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:17:50 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[A 50 bps jumbo rate hike can lead to financial stability concerns, hurt growth: Report]]> </title><description><![CDATA[SBI economists have lowered their rate hike expectations for the upcoming RBI policy review. They now anticipate a 0.25 per cent increase rather than the previously expected 0.50 per cent. This adjustment stems from concerns regarding financial stability and potential impacts on economic growth. The RBI's monetary policy committee is scheduled to meet from December 2 to December 4.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/a-50-bps-jumbo-rate-hike-can-lead-to-financial-stability-concerns-hurt-growth-report/articleshow/136130764.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-136130764,imgsize-334890.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/a-50-bps-jumbo-rate-hike-can-lead-to-financial-stability-concerns-hurt-growth-report/articleshow/136130764.cms</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:08:23 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Investors mint Rs 34.61 lakh cr in November as markets rally nearly 11%]]> </title><description><![CDATA[In a remarkable surge this month, Indian equity markets have observed a substantial upswing, with the BSE Sensex climbing nearly 11 percent. This rally was largely propelled by foreign institutional investors, who contributed record-setting inflows exceeding Rs 1 lakh crore. Motivated by lower crude oil prices and impressive Q2 earnings, investor optimism soared, although a recent profit booking saw a minor dip of nearly 2 percent.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/investors-mint-rs-34-61-lakh-cr-in-november-as-markets-rally-nearly-11/articleshow/136123662.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-136123662,imgsize-88698.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/investors-mint-rs-34-61-lakh-cr-in-november-as-markets-rally-nearly-11/articleshow/136123662.cms</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:28:46 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[HDFC Bank, Reliance Industries among 10 stocks with highest DII holding in Q2. See full list]]> </title><description><![CDATA[With the rise in the share of MFs and also an overall net investment of  Rs 1.69 lakh crore during the quarter, the share of Domestic Institutional Investors (DIIs) as a whole increased to an all-time high of 19.31% as on September 30, 2026, up from 19.16% as on June 30, 2026. Here are 10 stocks with the highest DII holding in the September quarter. ]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/hdfc-bank-reliance-industries-among-10-stocks-with-highest-dii-holding-in-q2-see-full-list/slideshow/136126992.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-136121710,imgsize-53170.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/hdfc-bank-reliance-industries-among-10-stocks-with-highest-dii-holding-in-q2-see-full-list/slideshow/136126992.cms</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:45:03 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[The LTCG debate: Why markets need tax stability and not ad-hoc fixes]]> </title><description><![CDATA[Foreign Institutional Investor capital is leaving Indian markets, raising concerns over the unpredictability of tax policies. Investors are urging for the reconsideration of Long-Term Capital Gains tax provisions. Historical changes in LTCG have created volatility that affects long-term investors negatively. A stable tax policy framework is essential to attract and retain investment in the Indian financial market.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/the-ltcg-debate-why-markets-need-tax-stability-and-not-ad-hoc-fixes/articleshow/136121257.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-136121257,imgsize-155174.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/the-ltcg-debate-why-markets-need-tax-stability-and-not-ad-hoc-fixes/articleshow/136121257.cms</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:38:55 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[India’s rupee has become an accidental carry star]]> </title><description><![CDATA[The Reserve Bank of India has made moves that temporarily attract carry traders to the rupee. Recent factors include decreasing oil prices and a shift in foreign investment from artificial intelligence stocks to Indian markets. However, these RBI incentives may not last, leaving uncertainty for traders. India's interest rate advantage has significantly diminished since 2011, raising concerns. Policymakers face challenges in ensuring sustained interest in the rupee amid historical depreciation.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/indias-rupee-has-become-an-accidental-carry-star/articleshow/136117132.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-136117132,imgsize-288542.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/indias-rupee-has-become-an-accidental-carry-star/articleshow/136117132.cms</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:13:12 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[NSEL releases Rs 1,950 crore in one-time settlement, ends 14-year payment default]]> </title><description><![CDATA[The National Spot Exchange Ltd has revealed a substantial settlement payout of Rs 1,950 crore to eligible claimants, marking the end of a lengthy 14-year legal battle stemming from a Rs 5,600 crore payment crisis. This settlement received the green light from the Mumbai bench of the National Company Law Tribunal, buoyed by considerable backing from claimants.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/nsel-releases-rs-1950-crore-in-one-time-settlement-ends-14-year-payment-default/articleshow/136104164.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-136104164,imgsize-31674.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/nsel-releases-rs-1950-crore-in-one-time-settlement-ends-14-year-payment-default/articleshow/136104164.cms</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:43:56 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Adani Airport raises $300 mn from 360 ONE Asset, taking total equity infusion to $1.35 bn]]> </title><description><![CDATA[Adani Airport Holdings Ltd will raise USD 300 million to enhance its presence in India's aviation sector. This investment will contribute to its target of increasing passenger capacity from 96 million to 200 million. The company operates eight airports, handling about 95.3 million passengers in the last fiscal year. The funds will support modernizing existing infrastructure and developing airport cities for commercial activities.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/adani-airport-raises-300-mn-from-360-one-asset-taking-total-equity-infusion-to-1-35-bn/articleshow/136104118.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-136104118,imgsize-71232.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/adani-airport-raises-300-mn-from-360-one-asset-taking-total-equity-infusion-to-1-35-bn/articleshow/136104118.cms</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:41:12 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cipla Share Price Live Updates: Cipla Stock Price History]]> </title><description><![CDATA[]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/stock-liveblog/cipla-stock-price-live-updates-23-nov-2026/liveblog/136092588.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-136092588,imgsiz